<title>NEW ZEALAND: MAX DOESN'T KNOW WHY SHARE PRICE FALLING.</title>
<headline>MAX DOESN'T KNOW WHY SHARE PRICE FALLING.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investor Max Resources Ltd said on Friday in a response to a New Zealand Stock Exchange enquiry it did not know why its share price had fallen 10.45 percent since close of business on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stock had dropped seven cents to 60 NZ cents per share.</p>
<p>Max said it was satisfied the market was fully informed, and noted the market price of Max resources had traded within a band of approximately 60-80 NZ cents in the past three months.</p>
